  "$comment": [
    "External tools: the single source of truth (spec §5.1).",
    "Read by the backend (src-tauri/src/services/manifest.rs) and by",
    "scripts/fetch_bundled_tools.mjs before the bundle is built.",
    "This file is tracked in git; the binaries it points at are NOT (spec §5.2.1).",
    "",
    "versioning:",
    "  latest  -> the asset is always downloaded from the newest release; `url` and",
    "            `sha256` stay null and the checksum comes from the release's own",
    "            SHA2-256SUMS. This is the only mode yt-dlp uses (spec §5.1).",
    "            `releaseApi` resolves the concrete tag (and records the version,",
    "            spec §5.2.1); `releaseUrl`/`checksumUrl` are the fallback for when the",
    "            API is unreachable or rate-limited.",
    "  pinned  -> `url` and `sha256` are both filled in and must match, byte for byte.",
    "",
    "Keys are Rust target triples, because that is what the bundler looks for",
    "(`externalBin`: <name>-<triple>[.exe], verified in tauri-bundler",
    "bundle/settings.rs::copy_binaries)."
  ],
